  "id": "stimulus-strength",
  "term": "stimulus strength",
  "definition": "Stimulus strength is the degree to which a presented stimulus is strong or weak during encoding, such as its contrast. In cognition research, it refers to a factor that affects the quality of perceptual and working-memory representations and can influence later task performance.",
